4. REPO FILES (~/Gezaji/Configs, owner: gezaji:gezaji)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Git stores only the executable bit. These are the modes it should record:

100755  bin/.local/bin/volume.sh
100755  bin/.local/bin/brightness.sh
100755  bin/.local/bin/wallpaper.sh
100755  polybar/.config/polybar/launch.sh
100644  everything else (configs, wallpapers, README.md, system/pkglist.txt,
        system/etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/30-input.conf)


5. SSH (owner: gezaji:gezaji)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
~/.ssh                                  700   drwx------  ssh refuses looser
~/.ssh/id_ed25519                       600   -rw-------  PRIVATE key, never share
~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub                   644   -rw-r--r--  public key, safe to share
~/.ssh/known_hosts                      644   -rw-r--r--  (600 is also fine)


6. CHECK EVERYTHING
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
stat -c '%a %U:%G %n' \
  ~/.config/i3/config ~/.config/polybar/config.ini ~/.config/polybar/launch.sh \
  ~/.config/dunst/dunstrc ~/.local/bin/*.sh ~/.vimrc ~/.bashrc \
  ~/.wallpapers/*.png /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/30-input.conf \
  ~/.ssh ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

Note: stat on a symlink path reports the symlink itself only with -L omitted.
Add -L (stat -L -c ...) to see the permissions of the real files they point to.


7. FIX EVERYTHING
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
chmod 644 ~/.config/i3/config ~/.config/polybar/config.ini \
  ~/.config/dunst/dunstrc ~/.vimrc ~/.bashrc ~/.wallpapers/*.png
chmod 755 ~/.config/polybar/launch.sh ~/.local/bin/*.sh
sudo chown root:root /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/30-input.conf
sudo chmod 644 /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/30-input.conf
chmod 700 ~/.ssh
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
chmod 644 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

After fixing permissions on files inside the repo, commit the change:
cd ~/Gezaji/Configs && git add -A && git commit -m "Fix permissions" && git push


8. WHY THESE MODES
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- 644 for plain config files: you can edit, everyone can read.
- 755 for anything that runs: scripts launched by i3 (exec) will silently
  fail without the executable bit.
- 700/600 on ~/.ssh and the private key: ssh ignores keys that other users
  can read, and prints "UNPROTECTED PRIVATE KEY FILE".
- /etc files stay root-owned: X reads them at startup; a normal user should
  not be able to change input or login behaviour system-wide.
